Core fix passes existing tests. Let me sanity-check the edge cases (page 0, past end, per_page 0, overflow) without touching the repo's tests.Fixed `src/lib.rs:4` with the minimal change:

```rust
pub fn paginate(items: &[i32], page: usize, per_page: usize) -> &[i32] {
    if page == 0 || per_page == 0 {
        return &[];
    }
    let Some(start) = (page - 1).checked_mul(per_page) else {
        return &[];
    };
    if start >= items.len() {
        return &[];
    }
    let end = start.saturating_add(per_page).min(items.len());
    &items[start..end]
}
```

Behavior now:
- 1-based pages: `start = (page - 1) * per_page`
- `page == 0`, `per_page == 0`, or `start >= items.len()` returns `&[]`
- Last page clamped with `.min(items.len())`, so partial pages work
- `checked_mul` / `saturating_add` avoid overflow panics for huge `page`/`per_page` values

Verification: `cargo test` → 2 passed, 0 failed (doc-tests too). Existing tests, signature, and doc comment untouched. I also ran a throwaway harness outside the repo covering `page 0`, page past end, `per_page 0`, empty slice, `usize::MAX` inputs, and `per_page` larger than the slice; all passed. Only `src/lib.rs` is modified (`Cargo.lock` generated by cargo was removed, since `.gitignore` only covers `/target`).
